SUMMARY:Resurrection of Our Lord Jesus Christ (Holy Pascha, Easter Sunday)
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260405
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260405T024822Z
UID:1fb71a702e4dfc663ee678c05ba699f841eb36a4@ordo.restorethe54.com
DESCRIPTION:Rank: Double First Class w/ Privileged Octave of the First Order\nColor: White\nFlowers: Yes, on all days for the rest of the liturgical year unless otherwise noted\nOrgan: Yes, on all days for the rest of the liturgical year unless otherwise noted\nCommemorations: This year, the feast of St. Vincent Ferrer, Confessor, is omitted.\nAfter Terce, Vidi Aquam replaces Asperges today and on all Sundays through Pentecost inclusive, no Commemorations, Sequence, Double Alleluia at the dismissal today through Saturday inclusive..\nGloria.\nCredo.\nPreface: Easter ("hac potissimum die")\nProper Communicantes/Hanc Igitur: Proper Communicantes and Hanc Igitur for Easter\n\nOffice:\n- Matins: Proper Office of the Easter Octave begins with Easter Sunday Matins and continues through None of Saturday.\n- Lauds: Proper Office of the Easter Octave, no Commemorations\n- Prime: Proper Office of the Easter Octave\n- Day hours: Proper Office of the Easter Octave\n- Compline: Proper Office of the Easter Octave\n\nWeb ordo info at: https://ordo.restorethe54.com/ordo/2026/4/5/\n
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holy Saturday
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260404
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260404T024822Z
UID:8bbdcb560af42d6370fac5be5b492d44cdc955ad@ordo.restorethe54.com
DESCRIPTION:Rank: Double First Class\nColor: Violet for the Vigil, White at Mass and thereafter\nPenance: Fast & Complete Abstinence until after Mass/Noon\nFlowers: Yes, at Mass and thereafter\nOrgan: Yes, from the Gloria of the Mass and thereafter\nCommemorations: This year, the feast of St. Isidore, Bp, Confessor, & Doctor, is omitted.\nPenitential kneeling: Only in the Office and Vigil before Mass\nAfter None, Blessing of the New Fire, Exsultet, Lessons, Blessing of the Baptismal Water, Litany of the Saints. After the Litany, Mass (in white) of the Easter Vigil, no Commemorations, no candles carried at the Gospel. After Communion, short First Vespers of Easter, no Commemorations. Double Alleluia at the dismissal..\nFolded Chasubles: Yes, at the Vigil before Mass\nGloria.\nNo Credo.\nPreface: Easter ("hac potissimum nocte")\nProper Communicantes/Hanc Igitur: Proper Communicantes and Hanc Igitur for Easter\n\nOffice:\n- Matins: Tenebrae on the evening of Good Friday\n- Lauds: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Prime: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Day hours: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Compline: Proper Compline for Holy Saturday. From now through None of Ember Saturday of Pentecost, the final Marian antiphon = "Regina Coeli", which is always sung standing.\n\nWeb ordo info at: https://ordo.restorethe54.com/ordo/2026/4/4/\n
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Good Friday
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260403
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260403T024822Z
UID:da136c1623e9efa5bbd03ae338c17b6eef4276dc@ordo.restorethe54.com
DESCRIPTION:Rank: Double First Class\nColor: Black\nPenance: Fast & Complete Abstinence\nFlowers are not permitted.\nThe organ is not played.\nPenitential kneeling.\nAfter None, Mass of the Presanctified. Lessons & Passion, Solemn Orations, Veneration of the Cross, Return Procession of the Blessed Sacrament w/ Mass of the Presanctified..\nFolded Chasubles are worn.\n\nOffice:\n- Matins: Tenebrae on the evening of Maundy Thursday\n- Lauds: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Prime: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Day hours: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Compline: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n\nWeb ordo info at: https://ordo.restorethe54.com/ordo/2026/4/3/\n
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Maundy Thursday
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260402
DTSTAMP;VALUE=DATE-TIME:20260402T024822Z
UID:6a17a0cbdff0155cde8a9c7e77f280fcf12bf86d@ordo.restorethe54.com
DESCRIPTION:Rank: Double First Class\nColor: Violet(Office),White(Mass)\nPenance: Fast & Partial Abstinence\nFlowers: Yes, for Mass only\nOrgan: Yes, until the Gloria of the Mass inclusive; silent thereafter until the Gloria of the Easter Vigil Mass\nCommemorations: This year, the feast of St. Francis de Paula, Confessor, is omitted.\nPenitential kneeling: Only in the Office\nAfter None, Mass of the Lord's Supper (bishops consecrate Chrism within this same Mass formulary), no Commemorations. Immediately after Mass, reposition of the Blessed Sacraement, Vespers, and then the Stripping of the Altars. Later, after the main meal has been taken, the Mandatum ceremony (optional) outside the sanctuary of the Church..\nFolded Chasubles are not worn.\nGloria.\nCredo.\nPreface: Holy Cross\nProper Communicantes/Hanc Igitur: Proper Communicantes and Hanc Igitur for Maundy Thursday\n\nOffice:\n- Matins: Tenebrae on Spy Wednesday evening. From now through None on Holy Saturday, special format of the Office for the Sacred Triduum. Only Matins & Lauds (=Tenebrae) are sung; all other Hours are recited without chant. From now until the Mass on Holy Saturday exclusive, the minor doxology "Gloria Patri" is completely omitted.\n- Lauds: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Prime: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Day hours: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n- Compline: Proper Office of the Sacred Triduum\n\nWeb ordo info at: https://ordo.restorethe54.com/ordo/2026/4/2/\n
END:VEVENT
